The test calls `probe.restart()`, where `probe` exposes `Qtile.restart`, `Qtile.dump_state`, and `Qtile._stop`. In `restart`, the non-error path is taken because the dummy core supports restarting and the test expects `config.load()` to succeed, so execution proceeds through the restart hook, lifecycle updates, opening the temp state file, and calling `dump_state`. `dump_state` pickles `QtileState(self)`, which runs `QtileState.__init__`: it initializes its fields, loops over three groups taking the `elif restart` branch for each non-`ScratchPad` group, then loops over two screens and updates `current_screen` when it reaches the current one. After returning from `dump_state`, `restart` stores the state file path and calls `_stop`, whose body logs, checks `_stopped_event`, and calls `set()` because the dummy object provides one.

